[agent] Done.
[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I logged the predictions to the Hopsworks platform and used its statistics capabilities to detect the distribution shift.
[agent] **Pipeline (all on-platform via `hops` CLI):**
[agent] 1. Created feature group `prediction_log` (v1) with schema `id:bigint, ts:bigint (event_time, epoch-ms), prediction:double, day:string`.
[agent] 2. Ingested all **13,621** logged predictions (`hops fg insert`) — the offline store materialized them as a Delta table (`delta.mlpaba3aea8_featurestore.prediction_log_1`).
[agent] 3. Computed per-day prediction statistics on the platform via Trino (`hops sql` → daily `COUNT`/`AVG`/`STDDEV`).
[agent] **Finding:** The daily mean prediction is stable at **~3.82–3.86** from 2026-01-01 through **2026-02-18**, then steps cleanly up to **~5.04** on **2026-02-19** and holds there for the rest of the log. The standard deviation stays ~0.30–0.31 throughout, so it's a pure level (mean) shift. The onset is sharp — a single-day jump between consecutive days.
[agent] **Deliverable:** `submission/answers.json` → `{"onset": "2026-02-19"}`
[agent] Notes on the interface: two small frictions were worked around within the CLI — the CSV `insert` path won't coerce ISO-8601 strings into the `timestamp` event-time type (used a `bigint` epoch-ms column instead), and Trino requires the global `--no-verify` flag plus discovering that cached FGs land in the `<project>_featurestore` schema under the `delta` catalog (not the default `iceberg.<project>`).
